  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1235 PM CDT Sun Jul 12 2026\n\nThe persistent, strong heat dome will remain over the region through \nthis week. Extended the heat headlines through Thursday evening for \nnow, even though Wednesday's HI values may be a little lower due to \nmore widespread breezy conditions. The wind and drier air with \nslightly lower dewpoints moving into central SD will result in both \nhigher actual temperatures and slightly lower \"feels-like\" \ntemperatures. However, southerly winds gusting 25 to 35 mph Monday \nwill also bring high fire danger to areas along the Missouri River \nas grasses cure. Issued a Fire Weather Watch for portions of north \ncentral SD for Monday afternoon with RH falling into the upper \nteens. Tuesday is actually the day with more widespread low RH, but \nwinds are more marginal so will need to evaluate fire concerns on a \ndaily basis going forward. \n\nThe core of the upper ridge finally begins to migrate south and east \nFriday into Saturday. A cold front trails through early Saturday but \ndoesn't seem to have any significant precip/moisture with it. Global \nmodels keep any showers to the north or southwest. Could potentially \nsee a break to highs in the 90s/100s the latter half of next weekend \nbehind the sfc cold front.",
